["Curious: does this also close https://github.com/bigchaindb/bigchaindb/issues/743 (seems like #875 supersedes #743?), based on the discussions that have happened?", "Curious: does `idx` stand for anything? In some ways `cid` still makes sense, since we're still talking about conditions inside an output, but I agree it might not be the best.", "Yea. I'll update #875 with the other changes that Dimi proposed. And yes I think this should count as resolving #743.", "Not quite, because it's: `tx.outputs[idx].condition`. I also considered:

* `oid`: sounds too much like 'object id'
* `output_idx`: Seems unnecessarily long. I got byte shaving ocd :grimacing: 
* `output_id`: Feels wrong to call it an ID, usually when we talk about an ID it's relative to the entire set of the thing in question, ie, the combination of transaction ID and output array offset is an output ID, which we are now calling `fulfills`...
* `offset`: Could also work...", "Hmm, I guess if it passed the eyeball tests of a few others, it's good.

My favourites below then, in decreasing descriptive-ness:

```json
{
    "transaction_id": "",
    "output_index": ""
}

{
    "transaction": "",
    "output": ""
}

{
    "txid": "",
    "output": ""
}

{
    "txid": "",
    "idx": ""
}
```

But let's not get hung up over this, I'll take what you like best 😄.", "So I'm not exactly sure why the tests are failing but I found another issue which needs to be fixed before merging:

https://github.com/bigchaindb/bigchaindb/blob/inputs-outputs/docs/server/source/data-models/crypto-conditions.md", "@username_2 https://github.com/bigchaindb/bigchaindb/pull/925/commits/7c12ee251dea8426b9653bd3bf63f8b4b1e6ca24", "@username_2 I've fixed your suggestions in b64026441ba83ca6bbeb806b90e2581a42c2501d and the backticks in 8470854769a93a7a7fcbd1b3282c136559d42460.", "I approved because I'm leaving on vacation soon and don't want my approval to be a blocker. I see you've resolved most everything I commented on anyway."]

