issue_description:
2 examples with a red dropShadow with blur. One of them has an outline stroke and the other one doesn't. 

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1453762/26885630-6eec72f0-4ba3-11e7-9b35-0889a36781ae.png)

```javascript
var app = new PIXI.Application(300, 300, {backgroundColor: 0x1099bb});
document.body.appendChild(app.view);

var style = new PIXI.TextStyle({
    fontFamily: 'Arial',
    fontSize: 36,
    fill: '#ffffff',

    strokeThickness: 5,

    dropShadow: true,
    dropShadowAngle: Math.PI/2,
    dropShadowDistance: 45,
    dropShadowColor: '#FF0000',
    dropShadowBlur: 5
});

var text = new PIXI.Text('Sample Text', style);
app.stage.addChild(text);
```

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1453762/26886007-8c2cb554-4ba4-11e7-9f09-b727eaa97244.png)

Same code without the strokeThickness set to 1. You can still see the drop shadow blur is red but the shadow itself is now black instead of red.


![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1453762/26885799-ecb3ee8e-4ba3-11e7-9148-322ccf0d65df.png)

Same code without strokeThickness. You can barely see the drop shadow blur but the shadow itself is now completely black.

